Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 49 CLINICAL DATA  Bilateral breast cancer by fine needle aspirate                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  SCANT BREAST PARENCHYMA WITH DISTORTED CYST LIKE STRUCTURE CONTAINING A DISLODGED FRAGMENT OF SLIGHTLY ATYPICAL EPITHELIAL CELLS  AND REACTIVE FIBROSIS   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The nature of the core biopsy specimen precludes definitive diagnosis  Multiple levels examined  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 51 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin in 2 separately labeled containers  Labeled  right   are 3  soft  tan pink cores of tissue ranging in size from a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in Cassette A  Labeled  left breast   are 3 ranging in size from a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in Cassette B  Gross Description by  Jason Corbin Resident  SAMANTHA J  PULLIAM  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 12 55 CLINICAL DATA  DCIS  with prior radiation for Hodgkin s                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  MULTIPLE FOCI THROUGHOUT THE LATERAL ASPECT OF THE BREAST  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  NOTE  Minimal invasion cannot be excluded  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  Despite extensive examination  only one lymph node was detected within the axillary soft tissue  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 10 54                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary sampling   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 3cm simple mastectomy specimen  with REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm of axillary tail and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm irregular overlying skin ellipse containing an eccenterically located nipple  The specimen is oriented with the short stitch marking superior and the long stitch marking lateral  The entire specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal dense fibrous breast parenchyma which has focally diffused gritty areas  in the right upper outer and right lower quadrants  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Many of these areas contain small firm cysts averaging in size 0 3cm  Two of thse gritty areas are frozen as FX 1  The closest of these gritty cystic lesions comes to within 0 9cm of the deep margin and 0 8cm to the closest anterior margin  There is also and ill defined white firm mass  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm located in the right upper outer quadrant adjacent to the axillary tail  The mass is 0 4cm from the closest deep margin and abuts the anterior margin  The small axillary tail is dissected for lymph nodes  several of which are found ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE SECTION CODE  A  FX 1  section of firm area  B  Gritty area and closest anterior margins  right upper outer quadrant  C  gritty area  closest deep margin  right upper outer quadrant  D  gritty area adjacent to frozen section  deep margin right lower outer quadrant  E  gritty area  anterior margin  right lower outer quadrant  F  gritty area  deep margin  right lower outer quadrant  lateral most  G  mass from right upper outer quadrant  anterior margin  H  mass from right upper outer quadrant  posterior margin  I  fibrous tissue  J  uninvolved breast parenchyma  K N  Possible lymph nodes  Resident  PAULA ARNELL  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  TWO SMALL NODULES   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  NO DEFINITE INVASION IDENTIFIED  O R  Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
