of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of unremarkable breast  all submitted in cassettes A through K  Representative section is frozen as FX 1 and kept frozen and will be sent to Cox 5  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm skin ellipse containing a 3 0cm  well healed scar and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm unremarkable nipple  Also attached to the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm axillary tail  No biopsy cavity is identified  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm firm  focally red and focally pink area which extends to 1 5cm of the closest deep inked margin  The rest of the breast parenchyma is focally white and focally yellow and grossly unremarkable  Section code  L  representative section of mass in relationship to deep inked margin M Q  additiona