Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Resident  Michael H Roehrl  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Erythema at right breast lumpectomy scar  showed angiosarcoma  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  ANGIOSARCOMA  GRADE 1 OF 3  MULTIPLE MICROSCOPIC FOCI  SEE NOTE  2  RECENT AND REMOTE BIOPSY SITES  3  CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH PRIOR RADIATION THERAPY  4  FOCAL MINIMAL FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FLAT TYPE   NOTE  Angiosarcoma is identified in several regions  including that of the periareolar scar  a superior medial scar  and in an area distant from both scars in the far medial breast  The tumor primarily involves the dermis but focally extends into the superficial breast parenchyma  In the most medial focus  angiosarcoma comes to 0 2cm from the superomedial skin margin  The remaining margins are  1cm away  Dr  Petur Nielsen has reviewed selected slides and concurs with the diagnosis  BREAST  RIGHT ADDITIONAL MARGIN UPPER FLAP   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT ADDITIONAL MARGIN LOWER FLAP   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  594 grams    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm mastectomy specimen  The weight of the specimen is 594 grams  The specimen has 2 undesignated stitches  with a long stitch presumably denoting the lateral and a short stitch presumably denoting the superior margins  Along the anterior aspect of the specimen  there is a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 7 5cm  In the center of the skin ellipse  there is a 3 4cm diameter areola with 0 6cm nipple  Along the medial aspect of the areola there is a periareolar scar measuring 2 4cm in length and 0 2cm in width  The scar is well healed and is several centimeters away from the closest margins  Along the upper medial aspect of the skin ellipse  there is another REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  well healed scar  This scar abuts the skin resection margin  Along the medial skin resection margin  there is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm area of slightly erythematous skin that abuts the resection margin  The deep resection margin consists of tan yellow  grossly unremarkable adipose tissue  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm area of tan white  slightly firm fibrous tissue that comes to within 0 5cm of the deep margin  This fibrous area is relatively well circumscribed  Within the fibrous area  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  slightly hemorrhagic area that is at 3 5cm from the deep margin and comes to within 2 0cm of the closest anterior deep resection margin  This area is approximately 1 5cm from the periareolar scar  The remainder of the parenchyma consists primarily of grossly unremarkable tan yellow adipose tissue without other focal abnormalities  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted are follows  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Periareolar scar  entirely blocked out  from superior to inferior   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest radial skin margin with respect to the periareolar scar  superior   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest radial skin margin with respect to the periareolar scar  inferior   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the second scar  from superior to inferior   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections