Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 48 CLINICAL DATA  49 year old female with infiltrating ductal carcinoma grade 2 with REMOVED_DATE nodes positive metastatic disease at the time of the left breast excision REMOVED_MONTH 4   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Positive margins for completion simple mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  ONE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS ADJACENT TO BIOPSY SITE  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FEW MICROSCOPIC FOCI  SURGICAL RESECTION MARGINS ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  2  BIOPSY SITE WITH FAT NECROSIS AND SUTURE GRANULOMAS  3  FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND LOBULAR EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma is similar in appearance to the previous resection  The in situ component focally exhibits pagetoid spread  which was seen in the prior resection  No perineural  vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 06                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number is a simple mastectomy specimen  with short stitches designating the superior margin and long stitches designating the lateral margin  weight 595 grams and 19 x 19 x 4cm with overlying skin ellipse 19 x 7 0cm with a surgical scar on the inferior outer border of the areola  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm biopsy cavity 0 5cm deep to the areola  filled with serosanguineous fluid 10cm from the right margin  12cm from the left margin  14cm from the superior margin and 3cm from the inferior margin  The biopsy cavity has a focal tan  smooth lining with areas of hemorrhage  Within the breast specimen are multiple foci of white tan unremarkable breast parenchyma  The axillary tail is not present and no lymph nodes are identified  There are no irregular  fibrous  gritty nodules within the breast tissue  Section code  A  lateral margin B  medial margin C  inferior margin D  superior margin E G  deep margin with biopsy cavity H J  representative sections of biopsy cavity K O  random breast tissue P  nipple Gross Description by  SCOTT O  URBAN  HMS Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 55 CLINICAL DATA  54 year old female with a history of ductal carcinoma on a recent biopsy of the left breast  who now presents for a lumpectomy and axillary node dissection                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  1  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE   15    MULTIPLE FOCI  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   85    CRIBRIFORM AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Intraductal and infiltrating ductal carcinoma are present within 1mm of the resection margins  3  SCAR TISSUE  FAT NECROSIS  AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION TO SUTURE MATERIAL  CONSISTENT WITH AN OLD BIOPSY SITE  LYMPH NODE  AXILLARY   DISSECTION  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA IN 7 OF 19 LYMPH NODES  WITH EXTENSION INTO PERICAPSULAR FAT Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 59                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number in two separate parts  Labeled  breast tissue  stitch inferomedial margin   is a 50 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  breast lumpectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm skin ellipse that contains a 3 8cm  longitudinal well healed scar  The specimen contains a long stitch in place designating the inferomedial margin  The specimen is inked in black entirely  and then inked in red on the medial surface  yellow on the lateral surface  and blue on the posterior surface  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a stellate  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  pink tan  gritty  firm area that is located 0 3cm from the anterior margin  1 2cm from the posterior margin  0 2cm from the lateral margin  0 2cm from the medial margin  8 0cm from the superior margin  and 1 5cm from the inferior margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is notable for unremarkable fibro  fatty breast tissue  The suspicious area is submitted entirely  Labeled  axillary nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is dissected to reveal nineteen lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 4 0cm in greatest dimension  The cut surfaces range from fleshy tan  to yellow  to white  SECTION CODE  A  superior margin  en face B  inferior margin  en face C  medial margin with mass  radial section D  lateral margin with mass  radial section E  anterior margin  radial section F  posterior margin  radial section G  mass with overlying skin H  mass  representative section I N  breast parenchyma  representative sections O U  axillary lymph nodes Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  AXILLARY   DISSECTION   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 06 CLINICAL DATA  Rule out breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  100    MODERATE TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures approximately 1 8cm in greatest dimension by gross examination  No definite vascular invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 35                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of pink tan fibrofatty breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal pink and white  shiny  semifirm cut surface  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in A through B  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  EXTENDING TO THE MARGINS  O R  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 03 CLINICAL DATA  Breast carcinoma in post menopausal female  Patient noted enlarged lymph node in the extreme lateral extent of the axilla  separately excised                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL ADENOCARCINOMA  2  MICROSCOPIC FOCUS OF ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH FIBROSIS  FAT NECROSIS AND FOREIGN BODY TYPE REACTION TO SUTURE  4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCYSTS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  NOTE  Thirteen of 13 axillary lymph nodes are negative for malignancy  The separately submitted  most lateral axillary node  and  separate axillary node  are negative for malignancy  The closest inked resection margin is negative for malignancy  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 20 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in three parts  Labeled  Right breast and axilla  is an 18 x 15 x 2 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen which includes a 14 x 8 5cm skin ellipse with a centrally placed 3 x 2 5cm areola and 1 3cm in maximum diameter nipple  4cm superolateral to the nipple is a 4cm well healed scar which is situated within 1 5cm of the closest inked superolateral margin  The remaining epidermal surface is unremarkable  The under surface of the specimen is smooth and glistening  however sectioning demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 2cm ill defined stellate firm mass with a centrally located 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm hemorrhagic area which is located subadjacent to the overlying epidermal scar  The mass is located 2cm from the closest deep margin and 3cm from the closest superior lateral margin  There is an attached 8 x 5 x 2cm axillary tail  The axillary lymph nodes are dissected from the surrounding fibroadipose tissue and a 5 x 5 x 0 4cm aggregate of tan brown lymph nodes are submitted entirely in A through E  Labeled  Most lateral axillary lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0 6cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is bisected and submitted entirely in F and G  Labeled  Separate axillary lymph node  is a 2 x 1 x 1cm portion of tan to yellow portion of lymph node and surrounding fibroadipose tissue  Bisected and submitted entirely in H  Section Code  A E  axillary lymph nodes  F G  most lateral axillary node  H  separate axillary node  I  closest deep margin  J M  representative sections of mass  N  scar  O  areola and nipple  P Q  representative suspicious areas away from mass  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  Robert Willard Carey  M D  PART A  BREAST AND AXILLARY TAIL  RIGHT  PART B  LATERAL AXILLARY NODE PART C  SEPARATE AXILLARY NODE   report_end  , Unchecked.
