 sectioned and  submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      B  Received fresh  labeled  left mastectomy   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm  mastectomy specimen with a short surgical suture designating the superior aspect  and a long surgical suture designating the lateral aspect  The specimen does  not contain any skin and is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm exposed defect within  the central specimen extending from the anterior to posterior surfaces  The  anterior margin is inked blue and the posterior margin is inked black  The rim  of the central defect is inked yellow  A gross photograph is taken  The  specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal several metallic  clips located within the region of the cavity  as well as red hemorrhagic soft  tissue surrounding the site of the prior excision  Surrounding the excision  site there is dense white fibrosis and the remainder of the specimen is made up  of yellow lobulated and unremarkable breast parenchyma  Representative sections  are submitted as follows     SECTION CODE    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of prior excision site  including anterior and  posterior margins    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections away from the excision cavity     C  Received fresh  labeled  left axillary lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  section of fibroadipose tissue containing a single nodular firm area measuring  2 9 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  This area displays pink white smooth cut surfaces and is  trisected and entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   along with the scant  remaining fibrofatty tissue           PART A  BREAST BIOPSY  LEFT DUCTAL TISSUE  PART B  BREAST MASTECTOMY  LEFT  PART C  LYMPH NODE  EXCISION  LEFT AXILLA       report_end  , Unchecked.
