ng REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The specimens are entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast  low axillary sampling   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  in which 12 lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  are identified  The lymph nodes and the remaining fibroadipose tissue are entirely submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 lymph nodes  1 inked black and bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of fibroadipose tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node  Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday May 05   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 08 47 38AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Patholo