Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 MAY 00 ACCESSIONED ON  10 MAY 00 at 11 14 CLINICAL DATA  50 year old female with invasive breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  RARE FOCI OF ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES INCLUDING SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND CALCIFICATIONS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 10 OF 10 LYMPH NODES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  12 MAY 00 at 18 00                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number is a 25 x 17 x 5cm mastectomy specimen with a 13 x REMOVED_DATE skin ellipse with unremarkable nipple  A 3 5cm well healed linear horizontal scar is present on the 6 o clock surface of the skin ellipse approximately 1 5cm from the nipple  A long stitch is present on the specimen demarcating the medial aspect and a short stitch demarcating the lateral aspect  As well a silk stitch is present on the attached axillary tail demarcating the highest axillary node  In the lower mid portion of the specimen directly behind the scar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm biopsy cavity with a smooth to focally granular hemorrhagic wall with surrounding ill defined tan yellow firm nodular tissue  The biopsy cavity and surrounding fibrous tissue changes approach the closest margin  anterior inferior  as close as 0 8cm  Throughout the remainder of the breast parenchyma are scattered tan white ill defined fibrous areas that are focally gritty  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 3cm in greatest dimension  SECTION CODE  A B  Representative sections of biopsy cavity and adjacent margin  mid posterior margin   C D  Representative sections of fibrous tissue surrounding biopsy cavity and closest  anterior inferior  margin  0 8cm grossly  E G  Further representative sections of biopsy cavity  H J  Representative sections of ill defined nodular fibrous areas within the breast parenchyma  the closest of which approaches the posterior margin  closest margin  0 6cm  K L   highest  lymph nodes  largest bivalved and half submitted  smallest are entirely submitted  M N  Mid portion lymph nodes entirely submitted  O  Lowest lymph nodes entirely submitted  Resident  AARON CAPLAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
